WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.600
Video nineteen. e-Invoice and e-Way Bill. Both
are in Beta.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.417
An e-invoice is a sales invoice that the
government's IRP registers.

00:00:10.347 --> 00:00:15.563
The IRP gives an IRN and a signed QR code.
They print on the invoice.

00:00:15.492 --> 00:00:18.377
An e-way bill goes with the goods on the road.

00:00:18.678 --> 00:00:23.230
Hisaab Services shows e-Invoice and e-Way Bill
with a Beta line.

00:00:24.282 --> 00:00:28.964
Hisaab tested them with a test copy of the
partner, not yet with the real service.

00:00:30.044 --> 00:00:34.327
Alt+Z opens Exchange. Send for e-Invoicing is
the first line.

00:00:34.924 --> 00:00:41.740
F2 sets the period. Hisaab sorts the invoices:
pending, corrections needed, and IRN generated.

00:00:42.439 --> 00:00:46.588
Invoice two has no PIN code of the buyer.
Correct it first.

00:00:46.618 --> 00:00:53.102
S sends the invoices online through Hisaab Services. X
exports the JSON for the bulk upload on the portal.

00:00:54.182 --> 00:00:59.532
The e-Invoice report lists each invoice with
its IRN, the Ack number and the Ack date.

00:01:03.653 --> 00:01:10.805
Open invoice 4, and press Ctrl+P. The IRN, the Ack
number and the signed QR code print at the top.

00:01:11.885 --> 00:01:18.902
Alt+Z, W opens Send for e-Way Bill. Hisaab lists what to
correct first: here, the PIN code and the distance.

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:25.165
Each e-way bill gets its number, its validity
and the vehicle number.

00:01:25.645 --> 00:01:31.394
In Beta, check each IRN and each e-way bill on
the portal. Next video: TDS.

